  "notes": "The stopped-rotor machine (PLAN \u00a70, Phase 5): a tip-prop rotor lifts it like the tipjet; slide the mode and the tip props die, the park controller brakes the head and indexes the blades spanwise, and the same two blades are now the WING - collective is wing incidence, pitch cyclic is the ailerons (at a 90-degree park, cyclic pitch is differential left/right blade incidence), the tailplane's elevator takes over pitch, and a pusher drives it. Slide back and the tip props spin the wing into a rotor again. Transition lift gap is real (it killed the X-50): convert high and fast.",
